Example: By next week, I will have completed all the assignments.
Watch out: Use will be + -ing for an action in progress at a future time, and will have been + -ing to focus on how long an action will have lasted.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say that an action will be finished before a particular time in the future."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a future deadline (by next week, by 2030, by the time you arrive)."},{"label":"Example","text":"By next week, I will have completed all the assignments."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use will be + -ing for an action in progress at a future time, and will have been + -ing to focus on how long an action will have lasted."}]', 130);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-01-002-01-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-01-002-01'), 'micro_feedback', 'A01-T06', 'Past Continuous (was/were + -ing)', 'When to use: To describe an action that was in progress at a particular moment in the past, often when something else happened.
Look for: at 9 p.m. last night, at that moment, while…, when the phone rang.
Example: I was studying for the test when the power went out.
Watch out: Use had been + -ing only when the sentence tells you how long the action had continued (for three hours).', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To describe an action that was in progress at a particular moment in the past, often when something else happened."},{"label":"Look for","text":"at 9 p.m. last night, at that moment, while…, when the phone rang."},{"label":"Example","text":"I was studying for the test when the power went out."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use had been + -ing only when the sentence tells you how long the action had continued (for three hours)."}]', 201);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-01-002-02-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-01-002-02'), 'micro_feedback', 'A01-T04', 'Past Perfect (had + past participle)', 'When to use: To show that one past action happened before another past action or time.
Look for: by 10 p.m., before she called, by the time the meeting started, already.
Example: By the time the meeting started, I had finished the report.
Watch out: If events are told in the order they happened, the simple past is usually enough (I finished the report and went home). Use had + past participle when you need to show which action happened first.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that one past action happened before another past action or time."},{"label":"Look for","text":"by 10 p.m., before she called, by the time the meeting started, already."},{"label":"Example","text":"By the time the meeting started, I had finished the report."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"If events are told in the order they happened, the simple past is usually enough (I finished the report and went home). Use had + past participle when you need to show which action happened first."}]', 202);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-01-002-03-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-01-002-03'), 'micro_feedback', 'A01-T05', 'Past Perfect Continuous (had been + -ing)', 'When to use: To show how long an action had continued up to a point in the past.
Look for: a past time or event (when she called, before the train arrived) together with a length of time (for two hours, for three months).
Example: By the time the train arrived, I had been waiting for two hours.
Watch out: Was/were + -ing only shows that an action was in progress, and had + past participle focuses on a finished action. Neither shows how long the action had lasted.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show how long an action had continued up to a point in the past."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a past time or event (when she called, before the train arrived) together with a length of time (for two hours, for three months)."},{"label":"Example","text":"By the time the train arrived, I had been waiting for two hours."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Was/were + -ing only shows that an action was in progress, and had + past participle focuses on a finished action. Neither shows how long the action had lasted."}]', 203);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-01-002-04-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-01-002-04'), 'micro_feedback', 'A01-T06', 'Past Continuous (was/were + -ing)', 'When to use: To describe an action that was in progress at a particular moment in the past, often when something else happened.
Look for: at 9 p.m. last night, at that moment, while…, when the phone rang.
Example: I was studying for the test when the power went out.
Watch out: Use had been + -ing only when the sentence tells you how long the action had continued (for three hours).', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To describe an action that was in progress at a particular moment in the past, often when something else happened."},{"label":"Look for","text":"at 9 p.m. last night, at that moment, while…, when the phone rang."},{"label":"Example","text":"I was studying for the test when the power went out."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use had been + -ing only when the sentence tells you how long the action had continued (for three hours)."}]', 204);
