Example: We will leave as soon as the rain stops.
Watch out: Do not use will inside the time clause for the future: as soon as the rain stops, not as soon as the rain will stop.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say when something happens in relation to another action: before, after, at the same time or up to a point."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"while / as = at the same time; as soon as / once = immediately after; until = up to that point."},{"label":"Example","text":"We will leave as soon as the rain stops."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not use will inside the time clause for the future: as soon as the rain stops, not as soon as the rain will stop."}]', 2104);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-021-05-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-021-05'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T02', 'Manner clauses (as if, as though, as)', 'When to use: To describe how someone does something or how something seems.
Look for: verbs such as look, act, sound or behave before the gap.
Example: He spends money as if he were a millionaire.
Watch out: When the situation is clearly untrue, use a past form: as if he were rich, not as if he is rich.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To describe how someone does something or how something seems."},{"label":"Look for","text":"verbs such as look, act, sound or behave before the gap."},{"label":"Example","text":"He spends money as if he were a millionaire."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"When the situation is clearly untrue, use a past form: as if he were rich, not as if he is rich."}]', 2105);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-021-06-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-021-06'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T03', 'Place clauses (where, wherever)', 'When to use: To say where something happens. where = a particular place; wherever = any place.
Look for: a clause about location without a noun like the place right before the gap.
Example: You can sit wherever you like.
Watch out: Do not add a preposition before where: Put it back where you found it, not Put it back at where you found it.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say where something happens. where = a particular place; wherever = any place."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a clause about location without a noun like the place right before the gap."},{"label":"Example","text":"You can sit wherever you like."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not add a preposition before where: Put it back where you found it, not Put it back at where you found it."}]', 2106);
