Watch out: such a heavy bag, not so a heavy bag; so heavy, not such heavy.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that something was so extreme that it caused a result."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"so + adjective/adverb (so heavy that); such (a) + adjective + noun (such a heavy bag that)."},{"label":"Example","text":"The bag was so heavy that I could not lift it."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"such a heavy bag, not so a heavy bag; so heavy, not such heavy."}]', 2227);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-022-28-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-022-28'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T06', 'Purpose (so that, in order to, in order that)', 'When to use: To explain why someone does something (the aim).
Key difference: in order to / so as to + base verb; so that / in order that + subject + can / could / would.
Examples: She left early in order to catch the train. She left early so that she could catch the train.
Watch out: Do not mix the patterns: in order to catch, not in order to she could catch.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To explain why someone does something (the aim)."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"in order to / so as to + base verb; so that / in order that + subject + can / could / would."},{"label":"Examples","text":"She left early in order to catch the train. She left early so that she could catch the train."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not mix the patterns: in order to catch, not in order to she could catch."}]', 2228);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-022-29-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-022-29'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T08', 'because of / due to + noun', 'When to use: To give a reason using a noun or noun phrase rather than a full clause.
Key difference: because of / due to / on account of + noun (because of the rain); because + subject + verb (because it rained).
Example: The match was cancelled because of the heavy rain.
Watch out: Do not put a subject and verb after because of: because of the rain, not because of it rained.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To give a reason using a noun or noun phrase rather than a full clause."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"because of / due to / on account of + noun (because of the rain); because + subject + verb (because it rained)."},{"label":"Example","text":"The match was cancelled because of the heavy rain."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not put a subject and verb after because of: because of the rain, not because of it rained."}]', 2229);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-022-30-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-022-30'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T04', 'Giving reasons (because, since, as)', 'When to use: To explain why something happens. because gives the main reason; since and as often give a reason the listener already knows.
Look for: a cause and a result in the same sentence.
Example: Since it was late, we took a taxi home.
Watch out: Use only one linking word: Because it was late, we left, not Because it was late, so we left.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To explain why something happens. because gives the main reason; since and as often give a reason the listener already knows."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a cause and a result in the same sentence."},{"label":"Example","text":"Since it was late, we took a taxi home."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use only one linking word: Because it was late, we left, not Because it was late, so we left."}]', 2230);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-01-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-01'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T09', 'Contrast with although / even though', 'When to use: To show that something happens despite another fact.
Look for: two ideas that seem to contradict each other, with a subject and verb after the gap.
Example: Although it was raining, we went for a walk.
Watch out: Do not add but in the same sentence: Although it was raining, we went out, not Although it was raining, but we went out.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that something happens despite another fact."},{"label":"Look for","text":"two ideas that seem to contradict each other, with a subject and verb after the gap."},{"label":"Example","text":"Although it was raining, we went for a walk."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not add but in the same sentence: Although it was raining, we went out, not Although it was raining, but we went out."}]', 2301);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-02-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-02'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T10', 'despite / in spite of + noun or -ing', 'When to use: To show contrast using a noun or an -ing form, not a full clause.
Look for: a noun or -ing form after the gap (despite the noise, in spite of feeling tired).
Example: Despite the noise, she fell asleep.
Watch out: No of after despite, and no subject + verb: despite the noise, not despite of the noise or despite it was noisy.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show contrast using a noun or an -ing form, not a full clause."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a noun or -ing form after the gap (despite the noise, in spite of feeling tired)."},{"label":"Example","text":"Despite the noise, she fell asleep."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"No of after despite, and no subject + verb: despite the noise, not despite of the noise or despite it was noisy."}]', 2302);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-03-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-03'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T11', 'Direct contrast (whereas, while)', 'When to use: To compare two different people or things side by side.
Look for: two clauses that show a clear difference (Tom is tall, whereas his brother is short).
Example: I prefer tea, whereas my sister prefers coffee.
Watch out: Both parts need a subject and verb: whereas his brother is short, not whereas short brother.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To compare two different people or things side by side."},{"label":"Look for","text":"two clauses that show a clear difference (Tom is tall, whereas his brother is short)."},{"label":"Example","text":"I prefer tea, whereas my sister prefers coffee."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Both parts need a subject and verb: whereas his brother is short, not whereas short brother."}]', 2303);
