Watch out: Do not add but in the same sentence: Although it was raining, we went out, not Although it was raining, but we went out.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that something happens despite another fact."},{"label":"Look for","text":"two ideas that seem to contradict each other, with a subject and verb after the gap."},{"label":"Example","text":"Although it was raining, we went for a walk."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not add but in the same sentence: Although it was raining, we went out, not Although it was raining, but we went out."}]', 2324);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-25-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-25'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T10', 'despite / in spite of + noun or -ing', 'When to use: To show contrast using a noun or an -ing form, not a full clause.
Look for: a noun or -ing form after the gap (despite the noise, in spite of feeling tired).
Example: Despite the noise, she fell asleep.
Watch out: No of after despite, and no subject + verb: despite the noise, not despite of the noise or despite it was noisy.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show contrast using a noun or an -ing form, not a full clause."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a noun or -ing form after the gap (despite the noise, in spite of feeling tired)."},{"label":"Example","text":"Despite the noise, she fell asleep."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"No of after despite, and no subject + verb: despite the noise, not despite of the noise or despite it was noisy."}]', 2325);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-26-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-26'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T09', 'Contrast with although / even though', 'When to use: To show that something happens despite another fact.
Look for: two ideas that seem to contradict each other, with a subject and verb after the gap.
Example: Although it was raining, we went for a walk.
Watch out: Do not add but in the same sentence: Although it was raining, we went out, not Although it was raining, but we went out.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show that something happens despite another fact."},{"label":"Look for","text":"two ideas that seem to contradict each other, with a subject and verb after the gap."},{"label":"Example","text":"Although it was raining, we went for a walk."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not add but in the same sentence: Although it was raining, we went out, not Although it was raining, but we went out."}]', 2326);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-27-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-27'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T12', 'Much as… (although I really…)', 'When to use: A formal way of saying although I really…, usually with feeling verbs such as like, enjoy, admire or want.
Look for: a strong feeling followed by a contrasting decision.
Example: Much as I enjoy working here, I have decided to leave.
Watch out: Follow Much as with a subject and a feeling verb: Much as I like him, not Much as the job or Much as I arrived late.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"A formal way of saying although I really…, usually with feeling verbs such as like, enjoy, admire or want."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a strong feeling followed by a contrasting decision."},{"label":"Example","text":"Much as I enjoy working here, I have decided to leave."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Follow Much as with a subject and a feeling verb: Much as I like him, not Much as the job or Much as I arrived late."}]', 2327);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-28-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-28'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T11', 'Direct contrast (whereas, while)', 'When to use: To compare two different people or things side by side.
Look for: two clauses that show a clear difference (Tom is tall, whereas his brother is short).
Example: I prefer tea, whereas my sister prefers coffee.
Watch out: Both parts need a subject and verb: whereas his brother is short, not whereas short brother.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To compare two different people or things side by side."},{"label":"Look for","text":"two clauses that show a clear difference (Tom is tall, whereas his brother is short)."},{"label":"Example","text":"I prefer tea, whereas my sister prefers coffee."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Both parts need a subject and verb: whereas his brother is short, not whereas short brother."}]', 2328);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-29-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-29'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T10', 'despite / in spite of + noun or -ing', 'When to use: To show contrast using a noun or an -ing form, not a full clause.
Look for: a noun or -ing form after the gap (despite the noise, in spite of feeling tired).
Example: Despite the noise, she fell asleep.
Watch out: No of after despite, and no subject + verb: despite the noise, not despite of the noise or despite it was noisy.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To show contrast using a noun or an -ing form, not a full clause."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a noun or -ing form after the gap (despite the noise, in spite of feeling tired)."},{"label":"Example","text":"Despite the noise, she fell asleep."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"No of after despite, and no subject + verb: despite the noise, not despite of the noise or despite it was noisy."}]', 2329);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-023-30-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-023-30'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T13', 'even if (a possible situation)', 'When to use: To say the result will not change, whatever happens.
Key difference: even if = a possible or imagined situation; even though = a real fact.
Example: Even if it rains tomorrow, the match will go ahead.
Watch out: Do not use will after even if: Even if it rains, not Even if it will rain.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say the result will not change, whatever happens."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"even if = a possible or imagined situation; even though = a real fact."},{"label":"Example","text":"Even if it rains tomorrow, the match will go ahead."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not use will after even if: Even if it rains, not Even if it will rain."}]', 2330);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-024-01-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-024-01'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T17', 'provided that, as long as, on condition that', 'When to use: To set a condition that must be met for something to happen.
Look for: permission or an agreement that depends on something.
Example: You can borrow my car as long as you drive carefully.
Watch out: Do not use will after these words: as long as you keep the receipt, not as long as you will keep the receipt.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To set a condition that must be met for something to happen."},{"label":"Look for","text":"permission or an agreement that depends on something."},{"label":"Example","text":"You can borrow my car as long as you drive carefully."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not use will after these words: as long as you keep the receipt, not as long as you will keep the receipt."}]', 2401);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-024-02-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-024-02'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T15', 'unless (= if… not)', 'When to use: To say something will happen if a condition is not met.
Look for: except if meaning in the sentence.
Example: You cannot enter unless you have a ticket.
Watch out: unless already means if not, so do not add a negative: unless you have a ticket, not unless you don''t have a ticket.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say something will happen if a condition is not met."},{"label":"Look for","text":"except if meaning in the sentence."},{"label":"Example","text":"You cannot enter unless you have a ticket."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"unless already means if not, so do not add a negative: unless you have a ticket, not unless you don''t have a ticket."}]', 2402);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-024-03-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-024-03'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T16', 'in case (to be prepared)', 'When to use: To say you do something as a precaution, because something might happen.
Key difference: in case = do it now to be ready; if = do it only when the event happens.
Example: Take an umbrella in case it rains.
Watch out: Do not use will after in case: in case it rains, not in case it will rain.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say you do something as a precaution, because something might happen."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"in case = do it now to be ready; if = do it only when the event happens."},{"label":"Example","text":"Take an umbrella in case it rains."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not use will after in case: in case it rains, not in case it will rain."}]', 2403);
