Look for: a first step that must finish before the next can happen.
Example: Once you finish your homework, you can watch TV.
Watch out: Do not use will after once: Once you finish, not Once you will finish.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say that one thing happens immediately after another is completed."},{"label":"Look for","text":"a first step that must finish before the next can happen."},{"label":"Example","text":"Once you finish your homework, you can watch TV."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not use will after once: Once you finish, not Once you will finish."}]', 2422);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-024-23-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-024-23'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T16', 'in case (to be prepared)', 'When to use: To say you do something as a precaution, because something might happen.
Key difference: in case = do it now to be ready; if = do it only when the event happens.
Example: Take an umbrella in case it rains.
Watch out: Do not use will after in case: in case it rains, not in case it will rain.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To say you do something as a precaution, because something might happen."},{"label":"Key difference","text":"in case = do it now to be ready; if = do it only when the event happens."},{"label":"Example","text":"Take an umbrella in case it rains."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not use will after in case: in case it rains, not in case it will rain."}]', 2423);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-024-24-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-024-24'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T17', 'provided that, as long as, on condition that', 'When to use: To set a condition that must be met for something to happen.
Look for: permission or an agreement that depends on something.
Example: You can borrow my car as long as you drive carefully.
Watch out: Do not use will after these words: as long as you keep the receipt, not as long as you will keep the receipt.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To set a condition that must be met for something to happen."},{"label":"Look for","text":"permission or an agreement that depends on something."},{"label":"Example","text":"You can borrow my car as long as you drive carefully."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Do not use will after these words: as long as you keep the receipt, not as long as you will keep the receipt."}]', 2424);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-05-024-25-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-05-024-25'), 'micro_feedback', 'A05-T17', 'provided that, as long as, on condition that', 'When to use: To set a condition that must be met for something to happen.
