Look for: here in the original words.
Example: ‘I like working here.’ → She said she liked working there.
Watch out: Change here to there when the report is made somewhere else.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"When you report words in a different place from where they were spoken."},{"label":"Look for","text":"here in the original words."},{"label":"Example","text":"‘I like working here.’ → She said she liked working there."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Change here to there when the report is made somewhere else."}]', 3519);
INSERT INTO feedback_items (feedback_code, test_id, test_part_id, question_id, kind, type_ref, heading, body, fields_json, sort_order) VALUES ('01-01-07-035-20-00', 1, 1, (SELECT id FROM questions WHERE question_code = '01-01-07-035-20'), 'micro_feedback', 'A07-T23', 'Reporting a first conditional', 'When to use: When reporting an if-sentence about a real future possibility.
Look for: both parts move back: if + present → if + past; will → would.
Example: ‘If you pass, you will get the job.’ → He said that if I passed, I would get the job.
Watch out: Change both verbs: if I passed, I would, not if I pass, I would.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"When reporting an if-sentence about a real future possibility."},{"label":"Look for","text":"both parts move back: if + present → if + past; will → would."},{"label":"Example","text":"‘If you pass, you will get the job.’ → He said that if I passed, I would get the job."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Change both verbs: if I passed, I would, not if I pass, I would."}]', 3520);
