Look for: claim, appear, seem, turn out, is believed, thrilled + an earlier action.
Example: She claimed to have discovered a solution.
Watch out: Use to have + past participle for an earlier action: thrilled to have won, not thrilled to win, when the win is already over.', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"When an action happened before the main verb or feeling."},{"label":"Look for","text":"claim, appear, seem, turn out, is believed, thrilled + an earlier action."},{"label":"Example","text":"She claimed to have discovered a solution."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Use to have + past participle for an earlier action: thrilled to have won, not thrilled to win, when the win is already over."}]', 3901);
