Look for: Only after…, Only when…, Only then, Only recently at the start.
Example: Only when the train stopped did we see the damage.
Watch out: Invert the main clause, not the when-part: Only when the train stopped did we…, not Only when did the train stop, we….', '[{"label":"When to use","text":"To emphasise that something happened only at a certain time."},{"label":"Look for","text":"Only after…, Only when…, Only then, Only recently at the start."},{"label":"Example","text":"Only when the train stopped did we see the damage."},{"label":"Watch out","text":"Invert the main clause, not the when-part: Only when the train stopped did we…, not Only when did the train stop, we…."}]', 4605);
